---
/* ===========================================================================
   /application-status — the page a disqualified applicant lands on.

   iClosed calendars support a per-event "disqualification redirect" URL,
   configured in the iClosed dashboard (the public API is read-only for event
   config, so that half of the wiring happens outside this repo — see
   docs/ECOSYSTEM_MAP.md and docs/booking-recovery/README.md §"Confirmation-
   page + disqualification settings"). This page is a candidate target for
   that setting on the social-media-consultation calendar used by /apply,
   /apply2 and /apply3. It is currently NOT wired up anywhere — the
   calendar's disqualification redirect URL is empty today (per
   booking-recovery/README.md), so nothing links here yet.

   iClosed's disqualification redirect appends the contact's PII to the URL
   (?iclosedEmail=&iclosedPhone=&iclosedName=). docs/booking-recovery/README.md
   documents a deliberate decision NOT to read that data — it belongs to the
   one cohort that must never be chased, since they were filtered out on
   purpose. This page follows that decision: it does not read, log, or
   forward any query string.

   Named to be discreet if a visitor glances at the URL bar (never
   "disqualified" or similar), reusing the pattern candidate-facing ATS
   portals use. Same visual system as the VSL pages (src/styles/vsl.css) —
   logo, eyebrow, headline, body copy — but deliberately WITHOUT their CTA
   button. A big "Apply Now" purple button under a decline message would be
   tone-deaf; the copy itself already tells the visitor what to do if their
   situation changes.

   No metaEvent: iClosed's own native Meta integration already fires the
   capitalized `Disqualified` event browser+server when this path is used
   (see docs/meta-ads/README.md §4). Adding a custom event here would
   duplicate that signal — the exact mistake the removed
   iclosed_potential/_qualified/_disqualified custom events made before they
   were pulled 2026-08-17.
=========================================================================== */
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/vsl.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Your Application — Synchro Social"
  description="An update on your Synchro Social application."
  bodyClass="vsl"
>
  <main class="as-page">
    <div class="as-wrap">
      <div class="as-brand">
        <img src="/images/logo.png" alt="Synchro Social" width="52" height="52" />
      </div>

      <div class="as-eyebrow">Application Update</div>

      <h1 class="as-headline">Thank You For Applying</h1>

      <div class="as-body">
        <p>
          Thank you for applying. Based on your responses, we don't think we're the right fit
          for each other right now.
        </p>
        <p>
          We work with established professionals who are ready to invest $2,000+ per month
          into their content and social growth.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your situation changes, please reach out again. We'd love to work with you when
          the timing is right.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="as-home-link" href="/">Return to homepage</a>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .as-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 100svh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--vsl-black);
  }

  .as-wrap {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 56px 24px 72px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .as-brand {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .as-brand img {
    width: 52px;
    height: 52px;
    display: block;
  }

  .as-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--vsl-p);
    margin: 0 auto 18px;
    padding: 0 12px;
  }

  .as-headline {
    font-size: clamp(26px, 4.4vw, 38px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.16;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 auto 26px;
    color: var(--vsl-ink);
  }

  .as-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .as-body p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(15.5px, 1.7vw, 17px);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--vsl-ink-dim);
  }

  .as-home-link {
    font-family: var(--vsl-font);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--vsl-ink-dim);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--vsl-border);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    transition: color 0.2s ease, text-decoration-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .as-home-link:hover {
    color: var(--vsl-ink);
    text-decoration-color: var(--vsl-p);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .as-brand,
    .as-eyebrow,
    .as-headline,
    .as-body,
    .as-home-link {
      transform: translateY(8px);
      animation: asRise 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.22, 0.61, 0.36, 1) forwards;
    }
    .as-brand { animation-delay: 0s; }
    .as-eyebrow { animation-delay: 0.03s; }
    .as-headline { animation-delay: 0.06s; }
    .as-body { animation-delay: 0.09s; }
    .as-home-link { animation-delay: 0.12s; }
  }

  @keyframes asRise {
    to {
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .as-wrap { padding: 40px 18px 52px; }
    .as-brand { margin-bottom: 28px; }
    .as-brand img { width: 42px; height: 42px; }
    .as-eyebrow { font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .as-headline { font-size: clamp(24px, 7.4vw, 30px); margin-bottom: 20px; }
    .as-body { gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  }
</style>
